diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index 52e51b5..d35da9d 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -17,6 +17,8 @@ and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0
 - `runs.jsonl` task snapshots and `plan-runs.jsonl` rows carry `over_building_ruled`: how many of the task's `validate_completion` calls had an `over_building` finding settled by an answer or a controller ruling instead of by a fix.
 - `anti-tangent-guard` 0.7.0 gains a fourth hook, `check-progress-nudge`: a `PostToolUse` hook on `Edit`/`Write`/`NotebookEdit` that asks a task for a `check_progress` call, once, when it has made ten edits since `validate_task_spec` without one. It reads the session's own transcript (a subagent's, or the main session's), refuses nothing, and is silent with no `validate_task_spec` call and after `validate_completion`. `ANTI_TANGENT_PROGRESS_EDITS` sets the threshold and `ANTI_TANGENT_PROGRESS_GUARD=0` turns the hook off; every failure allows. Trace lines read `progress | pass|nudge|skip | edits=N`, with the subagent in the session column.
 - The server writes `codescene-events.jsonl`: one content-free record for a `validate_completion` call whose `codescene` argument reports a run (`ran: true`, or raw `analyze_change_set` output). Within a task session a record is written only when the reported result differs from the last one recorded, so retries that resend the same result count as one run; a lightweight call records every time. The record holds `ts`, `tool` (`analyze_change_set`, or `other` for any other caller-sent name), `quality_gate`, `files_analyzed`, `verdicts`, `trend`, `net_pp` and `category_counts`; `skip_reason`, `skip_evidence` and `base_ref` are never written to it.
+- `validate_plan` takes an optional `plan_run_id`: the id an earlier round on the same plan returned. The round keeps that id, sends the reviewer only the tasks whose text changed since that round (heading and body, so a renumbered task counts as changed), carries every other task's result forward, and re-runs the plan-level pass only when the plan text changed, showing it the earlier plan-level findings so a resolved one is dropped and one that still holds keeps its id. A round in which nothing changed makes no reviewer call, whatever the stored verdict and however old the run. This round's `controller_rulings` and `controller_verified_references` are applied to carried results too, so adding a ruling costs no reviewer call. Changing `project_knowledge`, `mode`, the model or the attached `context_paths` reviews every task again under the same id. An unknown or expired id reviews the whole plan under a new run and adds a minor `plan_run_id` finding that names it; a truncated round keeps the id, leaves the stored review as it was, and returns `warn` with a major `reviewer_response` finding saying how many tasks have no result, so it cannot be read as a pass. Leave `plan_run_id` out to force a full review.
+- The `validate_plan` response carries `review_scope` — `revision`, `tasks_reviewed`, `tasks_carried`, `plan_level_reviewed` — and its summary block a `review_scope:` line. `events.jsonl` records `tasks_carried` on `validate_plan` events. A plan run has one header line per round in `runs.jsonl` and `plan-runs.jsonl`, under the same run hash, with `revision` (and `tasks_carried` in `runs.jsonl`); readers take the latest.
 
 ### Changed
 
